    "gradeBand": "4",
    "overview": "Solve comparison word problems with multiplication and division, and multiply bigger numbers.",
    "problems": [
      {
        "prompt": "A red ribbon is 6 inches long. A blue ribbon is 4 times as long. How long is the blue ribbon? Write an equation with a letter for the unknown number."
      },
      {
        "prompt": "Ella has 56 stickers. That is 7 times as many stickers as Dev has. How many stickers does Dev have? Write an equation."
      },
      {
        "prompt": "A school sold 145 fair tickets on Monday. On Friday it sold 3 times as many. How many tickets did it sell on Friday?"
      },
      {
        "prompt": "A giraffe is 18 feet tall. A child is 3 feet tall. How many times as tall as the child is the giraffe?"
      },
      {
        "prompt": "A bakery bakes 24 muffins on each tray. How many muffins are on 15 trays?"
      },
      {
        "prompt": "A farmer plants 38 rows of corn with 27 plants in each row. How many corn plants are there?"
      },
      {
        "prompt": "Maria has 12 shells. Ana has 3 times as many shells as Maria. Leo has 3 more shells than Maria. Who has more shells, Ana or Leo? How many more?"
      }
    ],
